+{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":131220,"duration_api_ms":134468,"ttft_ms":3330,"ttft_stream_ms":2897,"time_to_request_ms":361,"num_turns":9,"result":"I reviewed the eight authorized files for the stage35 recovery collection. Here is my read-only assessment.\n\n## Verdict: ACCEPT (as an independent re-collection protocol, not a recovery of old raw)\n\nThe contracts and plan preserve the frozen stage34/35 protocol and correctly treat the old collection as historical rather than archived. No code-level logic flaws that would invalidate a fresh run. The blockers below are operational preconditions, not defects.\n\n## Protocol preservation — confirmed\n\n- **Default native fused baseline**: both contracts define native as pinned local SequentialMLP + default weighted fused SwiGLU + fused causal softmax + native RMSNorm. The `training_argv` disables gelu/dropout/rope/grad-accum fusions but deliberately leaves masked-softmax-fusion at its default (on), so the fused softmax baseline stands. `run_performance.py:94` asserts `native_compiled_callables == {'weighted_swiglu': True, 'weighted_swiglu_back': True}`.\n- **Same-round control**: control = native + frozen CE0008 + gradnorm001; arms rotate within each seed and run sequentially in one round (ordering enforced at `run_performance.py:102-103`); promotion is strictly vs_control.\n- **Unchanged weighted004**: `b9a2ca76…` is consistent across plan, both contracts (`weighted_candidate_sha256`), controllers.json (long + experts `candidates/004`), and is hard-asserted in `run_audit.py:24`. `heldout_candidate_byte_identical: true`.\n- **Full gradients / FP32 masters / router proofs**: correctness checklist covers all main_grad tensors, all post-SGD FP32 masters at every step, BF16+FP32 masters at start; scope includes router probabilities/maps and probability gradients; probe/probe_offset/replay all run in the audit orchestration.\n- **Identical formal timer / seeds / gates**: timer = unchanged GPU-synchronized time.time, 120 steps, first 20 excluded, last 100 → ten interval-10 means; seeds (35102-04 long / 35202-04 experts, audits 35101/35201) and gates (gain > 1%, all three seeds faster) live in the byte-frozen contracts and are re-asserted in `run_performance.py:111`. Since contracts are among the 25 byte-identical controllers, seeds/gates are identical to the prior collection by construction.\n- **Pinning & storage**: native commit `5be9626…` in both contracts, `install_runtime.py`, and `run_performance.py`; runtime restored to original `/tmp` paths; captures/checkpoints to `/private` NFS; 25 controller files enumerated (13 long + 12 experts) match `all25_model_controller_files_byte_identical: true`.\n- **Old vs new separation**: `overwrite_original_records: false`, `original_raw_inventory_may_be_replaced: false`, status `frozen_before_fresh_model_training`, and raw_io_barrier #4 (\"a rerun is new evidence, not recovery of the old file hashes\"). The collection does **not** claim full archival — requirement satisfied.\n- **Raw-I/O discipline**: correctness raw transferred+SHA-verified locally *before* formal timing (barrier #2); `audit_and_profile_during_timing: false`; `run_performance.py:86` asserts no snapshots/activation/routing/profile dirs during timing.\n\n## Material blockers (must clear before GPU work)\n\n1. **NFS identity gate**: `install_runtime.py:21` aborts unless `Path('/private').resolve() == Path('/mnt')`. The new Pod's mount must resolve `/private → /mnt` or restoration fails. This is prerequisite #3 and is the hardest external dependency.\n2. **Archive completeness for restore**: restore requires a manifest with exactly 600 native sources + 25 byte-identical controllers, plus the bf16 `candidates/0008` and `/tmp/kda-gradnorm-stage26/candidate.py` referenced at `run_performance.py:79`. Native sources are reconstructible from the pinned Git blobs, but the archive/manifest must actually carry the bf16+gradnorm candidates — not verifiable from these files.\n3. **Original raw tensors are unrecoverable**: the Pod was replaced before full raw copy, so the old correctness raw cannot be fully restored. This blocks *recovering* old raw but **not** the new run — the plan intentionally mandates a fresh full audit. Prerequisites (SSH ingress + host-identity verify, platform Pod-data compare against the immutable inventory, NFS capacity/persistence) remain open.\n\n## Scope limitations of this review\n\n- **In-memory validator adaptation**: `run_performance.py:21-38` loads the sha-pinned `summarize_performance.py` and patches *only* the direct-launch argv gate, substituting exact outer-command equality + `formal_entry` check; the timing math, precision, model and native-interval checks are retained and the change is recorded via `adapted_sha256`. This is an intentional launch-gate adaptation, not an identical byte-frozen timer — flag it so reviewers don't expect a pristine validator.\n- **Shared backend**: the experts audit still validates `long/backend.py` / `long/backend-current.json` (40 sort-index probes) at `run_audit.py:25-27`; there is no separate experts backend. Consistent with controllers.json but worth noting.\n- **Joint-dimension experts model**: E4→E8 and S256→S512 move together; scope already disclaims this as not an isolated expert-count attribution.\n- I reviewed **declarations only** — no execution, no other files read. Pass/fail of the actual audits and timing is not assessed here.\n\nNet: the collection is a correctly-scoped independent re-collection that keeps the frozen baseline, control, weighted004, proofs, timer, seeds and gates intact while keeping old and new evidence separate. Clear the three preconditions before any GPU work.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a2c29a51-2ca7-4596-9391-2aaba734e4b0","total_cost_usd":1.2751035,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27274,"cache_read_input_tokens":10754,"output_tokens":9687,"server_tool_