+    "The bin-reuse bypass (bin[(gx,1,1)](current args)) relies on vendor Triton 2.4.1 CompiledKernel.__getitem__ producing a runner that launches c_wrapper with current tensors, runtime numel/N and the live stream. Candidate003's equivalent runner-call path passed all 48 replays with zero fallbacks, so this is low-risk, but if a future vendor build changes the runner arity, closure_ok flips and every launch degrades to the correct-but-slower JIT path, so the >1% gain gate may not be met even though numerics are unaffected.",
+    "do_not_specialize must actually drop both divisible-by-16 and equal_to_1 for numel/xnumel in this vendor so a single bin is valid for N==1 through N==256; the constructor/launcher source shows specializations skip do_not_specialize indices and configs.equal_to_1 is derived from the same specialization, which supports this, but if the vendor still specialized xnumel==1 separately the single-token expert would need its own key (still correct, just an extra compile).",
