+The first complete long9-process round failed its outer post-run resource gate because a process was still present. Its ownership/state was unresolved and it later exited. Preserve that original failed receipt and exclude that round from promotion. A full independent long resource-confirmation round uses identical candidate, controllers and timing rules. The external wrapper records process state, excludes only nonexecuting zombies, retains live-compute blocking and waits5s outside timing for process exit. BothGPU and CPU boundaries must be clear before and after accepted rounds. No other jobs were stopped.
